===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=i|へみ}}

{{IPAfont|⟨pe<sub>2</sub>mi<sub>1</sub>⟩}} → *{{IPAfont|/pəɨmʲi/}} → {{IPAfont|/pemi/}} → {{IPAfont|/ɸemi/}} → {{IPAfont|/hemi/}}

From {{inh-lite|ja|ojp|sort=へみ|-}}, from {{inh|ja|jpx-pro|sort=へみ|*papumi}}.

Derivation theories include:
* Possibly cognate with {{cog-lite|ko|sc=Kore|뱀||tr=baem|[[snake]]}}.
* Possibly related to, or influenced by, {{cog-lite|ojp|-}}-derived verb {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|食む||tr=hamu|to [[bite]]}}.
* Possibly also related to {{m-lite|ja|sc=Jpan|波布||tr=habu|a kind of poisonous [[pit viper]] native to [[Okinawa]]}}.
* Possibly related to {{cog|bsh|babísta}}, {{m|bsh|bibímsta|t=snake}} (< {{m|bsh||*pa-bǘm-stë|t=being in the ground}}).

